          "final_text_tail": "re-existing litellm issues, verified against unmodified code), ruff format is clean (the one lint warning is pre-existing).\n\n**Changes in `dspy/adapters/types/tool.py`:**\n\n*Task 1 \u2014 flexible parsing:*\n- `ToolCalls.validate_input(data)` (tool.py:303): classmethod returning normalized Python structures, never a `ToolCalls` instance \u2014 dict with `tool_calls` as-is, single `{\"name\", \"args\"}` dict as-is, bare list as-is, JSON strings parsed to their dict/list, non-JSON strings returned unchanged.\n- `_normalize_input` (tool.py:334): pydantic `model_validator(mode=\"before\")` that calls `validate_input` then wraps single objects and bare lists into `{\"tool_calls\": [...]}` so `ToolCalls` instances construct correctly from every format (including a single dict nested under `tool_calls`). This makes all adapter parse paths work end-to-end.\n\n*Task 2 \u2014 deterministic fingerprinting:*\n- `_canonicalize_tool_call_args` (tool.py:260): recursively sorts dict keys, converts tuples to lists, strips string whitespace, leaves numbers/booleans/None untouched.\n- `ToolCall` (tool.py:284): new `fingerprint: str` and `id: str` fields, computed once in `__init__` (tool.py:290) as SHA-256 hex of `json.dumps({\"name\": ..., \"args\": <canonicalized>}, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))`; `id` is the first 8 chars. Verified stable across key order, whitespace, and tuple/list differences, and sensitive to `name`/arg changes; works via `from_dict_list`, direct construction, `model_validate`, and `TypeAdapter`.",
